WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.967
-Good evening. I'm Seth Meyers

00:00:01.967 --> 00:00:02.968
and this is "Late Night."

00:00:02.968 --> 00:00:03.970
How's everybody in the

00:00:03.970 --> 00:00:05.205
Mountain time zone

00:00:05.205 --> 00:00:07.006
[ Laughter ]
doing tonight?

00:00:07.006 --> 00:00:08.541
Let's get to the news.

00:00:08.541 --> 00:00:10.977
After an aide told
former President Trump

00:00:10.977 --> 00:00:14.147
that there was no legal recourse
to stop late night comedy shows

00:00:14.147 --> 00:00:15.782
from making fun of him,
Trump reportedly asked,

00:00:15.782 --> 00:00:18.317
"Can something else be done
about it?"

00:00:18.317 --> 00:00:21.454
Well, Donald, I'm pleased
to announce the answer is yes.

00:00:21.454 --> 00:00:22.455
Here is my offer.

00:00:22.455 --> 00:00:24.224
When Broadway comes back
in the fall,

00:00:24.224 --> 00:00:26.926
you play Willy Loman
in "Death of a Salesman."

00:00:26.926 --> 00:00:28.928
That's it.
That's all you have to do.

00:00:28.928 --> 00:00:31.797
If you play Willy Loman
in "Death of a Salesman,"

00:00:31.797 --> 00:00:33.799
we will not make fun of you
on "Late Night"

00:00:33.799 --> 00:00:34.801
for the rest of the year.

00:00:34.801 --> 00:00:36.769
But you have to be off-book.

00:00:36.769 --> 00:00:38.338
If you forget your lines,
or, more likely,

00:00:38.338 --> 00:00:39.672
don't read the script,
in the first place,

00:00:39.672 --> 00:00:41.574
you just have
to make something up.

00:00:41.574 --> 00:00:43.042
You just have to make up a plot

00:00:43.042 --> 00:00:44.243
of whatever you think

00:00:44.243 --> 00:00:46.879
[ Laughter ]
"Death of a Salesman" is about.

00:00:46.879 --> 00:00:49.115
And, if you're wondering what
the catch is, there isn't one.

00:00:49.115 --> 00:00:51.050
This is just something
I personally

00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:52.652
would really enjoy seeing.

00:00:52.652 --> 00:00:54.320
But if you don't do this,
well, then, I'm sorry,

00:00:54.320 --> 00:00:57.790
but it's eclipse city in the
graphics department, baby.

00:00:57.790 --> 00:00:59.993
[ Laughter ]
The White House
yesterday announced

00:00:59.993 --> 00:01:01.427
which countries will receive

00:01:01.427 --> 00:01:03.997
55 million doses
of the coronavirus vaccine.

00:01:03.997 --> 00:01:06.766
And they were
pretty dramatic about it.

00:01:06.766 --> 00:01:08.734
-Argentina!

00:01:08.734 --> 00:01:09.802
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:01:09.802 --> 00:01:11.236
Brazil!

00:01:11.236 --> 00:01:12.238
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:01:12.238 --> 00:01:13.539
Colombia!

00:01:13.539 --> 00:01:15.508
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:01:15.508 --> 00:01:16.943
-The Senate voted today

00:01:16.943 --> 00:01:18.844
on the For the People
voting rights bill.

00:01:18.844 --> 00:01:22.648
Republicans voted from the floor
between 6:00 am and 6:00 pm,

00:01:22.648 --> 00:01:24.984
and Democrats voted
at an elementary school

00:01:24.984 --> 00:01:28.254
30 miles away,
between noon and 12:15 pm.

00:01:28.254 --> 00:01:30.690
New York prosecutors
are reportedly investigating

00:01:30.690 --> 00:01:32.925
if Trump Organization
executives --

00:01:32.925 --> 00:01:35.261
excuse me --
executive Matthew Calamari

00:01:35.261 --> 00:01:37.730
received tax-free benefits
from the company.

00:01:37.730 --> 00:01:40.600
Prosecutors aren't sure
if they really want Calamari,

00:01:40.600 --> 00:01:42.235
or if he's just something
to pick at

00:01:42.235 --> 00:01:44.070
while they wait
for the main course.

00:01:44.070 --> 00:01:45.171
Do you get it?

00:01:45.171 --> 00:01:47.173
[ Laughter ]
Oh, were you running lines

00:01:47.173 --> 00:01:48.440
for "Death of a Salesman?"

00:01:48.440 --> 00:01:49.575
[ Laughs ]

00:01:49.575 --> 00:01:51.276
Texas Governor Greg Abbott
last week

00:01:51.276 --> 00:01:52.678
signed a bill into law

00:01:52.678 --> 00:01:55.381
allowing residents to carry
a handgun without a license.

00:01:55.381 --> 00:01:58.017
So, the next time
the electrical grid collapses,

00:01:58.017 --> 00:02:01.153
you'll at least feel
like you have power.

00:02:01.153 --> 00:02:02.855
During a tele town hall
yesterday

00:02:02.855 --> 00:02:04.891
about the For the People
voting rights bill,

00:02:04.891 --> 00:02:08.561
former President Barack Obama
urged Senate Republicans not

00:02:08.561 --> 00:02:11.831
to use the filibuster to block
a vote on the legislation.

00:02:11.831 --> 00:02:14.167
Oh, yeah, well,
I'm sure they'll listen to you.

00:02:14.167 --> 00:02:16.235
Why not have Hillary
and the cast of "Pose"

00:02:16.235 --> 00:02:17.403
give them a call as well?

00:02:17.403 --> 00:02:18.504
[ Laughter ]

00:02:18.504 --> 00:02:20.172
President Biden
is reportedly planning

00:02:20.172 --> 00:02:23.209
to announce a strategy to reduce
gun violence this summer,

00:02:23.209 --> 00:02:25.578
but, before you give him
too much credit,

00:02:25.578 --> 00:02:27.680
the plan is free knives.

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:28.814
[ Laughter ]

00:02:28.814 --> 00:02:30.549
In a new interview,
Senator Joe Manchin

00:02:30.549 --> 00:02:31.784
described growing up

00:02:31.784 --> 00:02:34.086
in a big, Italian,
Appalachian family and said,

00:02:34.086 --> 00:02:36.556
"I didn't care
what color you were.

00:02:36.556 --> 00:02:38.257
I'm going to hug
and kiss you, first,

00:02:38.257 --> 00:02:40.426
and then find out
if we're related."

00:02:40.426 --> 00:02:41.794
[ As Giuliani ]
I go further than that!

00:02:41.794 --> 00:02:43.028
Said Rudy Giuliani.

00:02:43.028 --> 00:02:45.164
[ Laughter ]
And, again,

00:02:45.164 --> 00:02:47.233
I really need to hammer home

00:02:47.233 --> 00:02:48.935
this man married his cousin.

00:02:48.935 --> 00:02:50.637
His second cousin.

00:02:50.637 --> 00:02:52.372
He was married to a cousin,
divorced her,

00:02:52.372 --> 00:02:53.840
and married a second cousin.

00:02:53.840 --> 00:02:55.041
[ Laughter ]
Oh, oh.

00:02:55.041 --> 00:02:56.442
Oh, second cousin.

00:02:56.442 --> 00:02:57.844
But you believed it
for a second.

00:02:57.844 --> 00:02:59.679
[ Laughter ]

00:02:59.679 --> 00:03:02.248
While campaigning yesterday,
New York mayoral hopeful

00:03:02.248 --> 00:03:04.450
and Brooklyn Borough President
Eric Adams

00:03:04.450 --> 00:03:08.520
called rival candidate
Andrew Yang a fraud and a liar.

00:03:08.520 --> 00:03:11.590
And then, Andrew Yang
called Brooklyn, "Brooklyin'."

00:03:11.590 --> 00:03:13.326
Am I saying that right?
I think that's right.

00:03:13.326 --> 00:03:14.393
[ Laughter ]

00:03:14.393 --> 00:03:15.394
The members of the first

00:03:15.394 --> 00:03:17.029
U.S. Olympic Skateboarding Team

00:03:17.029 --> 00:03:19.465
were announced yesterday,
though I'd probably remind them

00:03:19.465 --> 00:03:21.334
as it gets closer.

00:03:21.334 --> 00:03:23.669
[ Laughter ]
Delta Airlines
announced yesterday

00:03:23.669 --> 00:03:25.370
that it expects to hire

00:03:25.370 --> 00:03:27.707
over 1,000 pilots
by next summer,

00:03:27.707 --> 00:03:29.942
in order to meet
the growing travel demand.

00:03:29.942 --> 00:03:32.412
Though this isn't
very reassuring --

00:03:32.412 --> 00:03:33.913
[ Laughter ]

00:03:33.913 --> 00:03:36.882
Amid a national shortage
of chicken wings,

00:03:36.882 --> 00:03:40.319
restaurant chain Wingstop
has launched an online brand,

00:03:40.319 --> 00:03:43.222
selling chicken thighs,
called Thighstop.

00:03:43.222 --> 00:03:44.590
And things were even tougher

00:03:44.590 --> 00:03:46.793
over at Buffalo Wild Beaks.

00:03:46.793 --> 00:03:50.429
[ Laughter ]

00:03:50.429 --> 00:03:55.234
Las Vegas Raiders defensive end
Carl Nassib yesterday

00:03:55.234 --> 00:03:57.269
became the first active
NFL player in history

00:03:57.269 --> 00:03:58.437
to come out as gay.

00:03:58.437 --> 00:04:00.306
Said fans, "What?!

00:04:00.306 --> 00:04:03.809
The Raiders play in Vegas now?!"

00:04:03.809 --> 00:04:05.845
And, finally,
according to new study,

00:04:05.845 --> 00:04:08.280
men who are unhappy
in their marriages are

00:04:08.280 --> 00:04:09.581
at a higher risk of death.

00:04:09.581 --> 00:04:12.484
As for men who are happy
in their marriages, why,

00:04:12.484 --> 00:04:13.786
they're dead already.

00:04:13.786 --> 00:04:15.020
[ Laughter ]
Baze.

00:04:15.020 --> 00:04:16.289
Oh, I'm glad you laughed, Baze.

00:04:16.289 --> 00:04:17.656
[ Laughter ]

00:04:17.656 --> 00:04:18.925
Put me out there.

00:04:18.925 --> 00:04:20.026
[ Laughter ]

00:04:20.026 --> 00:04:21.394
And that, you guys,
was the monologue.

